# krome_init_abund.dat — Archean Earth (~2.5 Ga, pre-GOE) target
#
# Used when INITAB=1, exactly like krome_init_abund_earth_modern_N2O2CO2CH4.dat
# (see that file's header for the mechanism: krome_init_abund_on forces
# these species' mixing ratios back to the listed values at EVERY layer,
# EVERY outer iteration -- marcs.f INITAB overwrite loop -- standing in for
# the biological/geological fluxes that buffer them in the real atmosphere,
# since gas-phase equilibrium/non-eq chemistry alone can't sustain them.
#
# IMPORTANT: this pinning is the dominant control on N2/O2/CO2/CH4 (and, as
# of 2026-09-13, H2O) in this model -- elemental abundances (elabund)
# matter for the remaining FREE species (O3, CO, OH, NOx, ...) that GGchem
# computes from the elemental budget, but NOT for these 5, since their
# GGchem-computed values get overwritten unconditionally every iteration
# regardless of elabund. Confirmed empirically: test59 (elabund O
# 13.926->13.32, a 0.6 dex elemental shift) moved bulk O2 by only
# ~0.01-0.05 (0.20-0.26 -> 0.19-0.20), because O2 was pinned to 0.20946
# throughout in both runs.
#
# --- Sources for the Archean targets below ---
# Catling & Zahnle 2020, "The Archean atmosphere", Science Advances 6,
# eaax1420 (https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.aax1420):
#   - O2 < 1e-6 PAL (PAL = 0.20946) -- essentially anoxic, pre-GOE
#     (GOE ~2.4 Ga; 2.5 Ga sits just before it)
#   - N2 similar to today, or up to a few times lower
#   - CO2 ~10-2500x modern; geological (paleosol/rainwater) constraints
#     at ~2.5 Ga specifically: ~3-25 mbar (Catling & Zahnle's own
#     compiled range); other paleosol methods (Kanzaki & Murakami 2015)
#     give 85-510 PAL at 2.77 Ga -- wide spread, picked the ~2.5 Ga
#     paleosol range as the anchor since it's the best-dated/-constrained
#     Neoarchean point closest to pre-GOE.
#   - CH4 ~100-1e4x modern (modern ~1.8 ppm); pCH4:pCO2 ~0.1 is the
#     modeled warming optimum (Charnay et al.-type Archean climate runs)
#     and also roughly the threshold above which organic haze forms --
#     used as the CH4/CO2 ratio anchor rather than picking CH4 in
#     isolation.
#
# --- Fixed bulk reservoir species (Archean, ~2.5 Ga, pre-GOE) ---
# 2026-10-08: N2 set to the REMAINDER (1 - O2 - CO2 - CH4 - H2O) instead
# of the modern value, so these 5 pinned species sum to exactly 1 --
# closing the ~20.9% gap this file used to leave open (see former
# CAVEAT below, kept for history). PTARGET-DIAG (boundary_layer_mass_
# balance_issue investigation) confirmed msum/target was flatlining at
# ~0.7918 every call because nothing was filling that gap now that
# GAPFILL (unstable, reverted) is gone -- N2 is the obvious sink since
# Catling & Zahnle 2020 only constrain it to "similar to today, or up
# to a few times lower," i.e. this absorption is within the cited
# uncertainty, unlike O2/CO2/CH4 which have their own dedicated proxy
# constraints.
N2        9.8900E-01   # = 1 - (O2+CO2+CH4+H2O), was 7.8084E-01 (modern value)
O2        1.0000E-07   # deep anoxic, <1e-6 PAL (PAL O2 = 0.20946)
CO2       1.0000E-02   # ~1%, ~10 mbar-equivalent, mid of the ~2.5 Ga paleosol range (3-25 mbar)
CH4       1.0000E-03   # ~1000 ppm; pCH4:pCO2 = 0.1 (warming optimum / haze onset), within 100-1e4x modern envelope
H2O       3.0000E-06   # 2026-09-13: dry cold-trap value (~3 ppm, modern stratospheric H2O),
#                        NOT a surface humidity value. Without condensation/cold-trap physics,
#                        GGchem was instead filling H2O in to make up the ~21% gap left by
#                        pinning O2 far below modern (see CAVEAT below) -- found post-run to
#                        reach ~2.9% VMR at the top of the atmosphere (layer 1) vs ~0.17% at
#                        the surface (layer 100), backwards from real Earth and almost
#                        certainly driving unrealistic H2O-photolysis-sourced OH production
#                        (H2O2/OH/HNO3/HNO2 were seen swinging 3-8x between chemistry
#                        updates). Pinning to the dry upper-atmosphere value everywhere is a
#                        compromise -- it removes the runaway high-altitude H2O but also
#                        removes any realistic surface humidity, since one INITAB value can't
#                        represent both a moist surface and a dry, cold-trapped upper
#                        atmosphere at once.
#
# All other species (O3, N2O, CO, H2, SO2, H2S, O, H, OH, HO2, NO,
# NO2, etc.) default to 1E-20 initial guess and evolve to whatever GGchem
# equilibrium + KROME non-eq photochemistry + eddy mixing produce.
#
# FORMER CAVEAT (resolved 2026-10-08, kept for history): this file used
# to pin N2 at the modern value, leaving N2+O2+CO2+CH4+H2O summing to
# only ~0.791 (vs modern's ~0.991) -- a ~20.9% gap where modern's O2
# used to be. The original plan was for GGchem's own equilibrium
# allocation among the "free" species (O3, CO, H2, etc.) to fill that
# gap -- but PTARGET-DIAG confirmed it never did (msum/target flatlined
# at ~0.7918 every call, every layer, no matter how many iterations
# ran), and GAPFILL (the mechanism built specifically to redistribute
# that gap to the free species) turned out to be numerically unstable
# (T-correction blowups, 2026-10-08) and was reverted. N2 now absorbs
# the remainder directly instead, per the note above. Geological
# pressure-proxy work (Som et al. 2012/2016) arguing Archean total
# surface pressure was itself LOWER than today remains a more
# physically-motivated alternative fix (reduce PPE instead of inflating
# N2), not yet attempted here due to PPE's own fragility history
# (TRYCK/PPE cap work). See also the parallel elabund investigation
# (standalone GGchem) aimed at finding an elemental budget that
# reproduces a more realistic archean bulk composition independent of
# this pinning file's choices.
